6-389b-4ca6-bc3c-6612a0503fac"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"348e1236fb5abb9bbdc7f9a36a4ce856f5f46ffccf16dcff528905692c9f3633","event_uuid":"d6ed9a12-b037-46b5-8b30-a5ec73641315","position":{"commit_sha":"0f4ed3b0f0f65dcb0a6f8bb59eb36f590fb11091","position":"1786730756668164001-d6ed9a12-b037-46b5-8b30-a5ec73641315"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation pushed as Gerrit change 1781 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1781), base = current origin/main (post-1771).\n\nWHAT LANDED\n- Terminal fold at archive time: leaf.archive() now calls _terminal_fold() right before writing the ARCHIVED event — reuses compact_cli with --threshold=0 --horizon=0 --skip-sync (gates bypassed via existing flags; ZERO compact_txn.py diff, so no conflict surface with winning-endurant-xenops). No-op guard via compact._foldable_event_count(dir, now, 0)==0 (no empty/duplicate SNAPSHOT on a settled ticket); fold rc!=0 raises CommandError and aborts the archive. Push rides the ARCHIVED event's write_and_push.\n- Active-only scoping: fsck_repair._ticket_dirs(tracker, *, include_archived=False) is the shared iterator; skip only when .archived marker exists AND reducer._api._is_net_archived confirms (marker alone never decides — new _dir_is_archived helper). fsck_scan's four per-ticket checks + _scan thread include_archived; fsck.py parses/strips --include-archived (works with --output json, threaded through --repair's post-scan too); compact.py _scan_snapshot_state now walks via the shared iterator (return contract kept), _compact_all_parse/compact_all_cli thread --include-archived. Usage lines in _cli/help/fsck.txt + compact-all.txt; docs/user-guide.md gained an 'Archived tickets: maintenance scopes to the active store' section.\n\nEVIDENCE\n- RED-first: 7 of 10 new tests failed on unmodified code (archive left log unfolded; walks visited archived dirs; flag unknown → OutputFormatError/exit); tests/unit/test_scan_scoping.py now 10/10 GREEN. Edges covered: stale-marker + reverted-archive (ARCHIVED+REVERT) still visited by default; corrupt event in archived ticket invisible by default / reported (text+JSON, rc 1) with the flag; legacy-archived unfolded ticket selected+folded only by compact-all --include-archived; settled-ticket archive writes no new SNAPSHOT; empty store clean.\n- Manual mutation pass: 9/9 KILLED (marker-only decision, inverted include_archived, terminal fold keeping incremental gates, guard dropped, fold skipped, flag-threading dropped in compact_all_cli and fsck_cli, usage line lost, _scan_snapshot_state ignoring its parameter).\n- Gates: make lint clean (complexity ratchet active=53 new=0 increased=0; raw-git gate clean — no raw git writes added), make typecheck clean (mypy 539 files), adjacent suites 304 passed (-k 'fsck or compact or archive or leaf or scan') + 70 passed in repair-pause/archived-roundtrip/marker suites (the _ticket_dirs monkeypatch sites unaffected).\n\nAwaiting LLM-Review + Verified on 1781; will rebase if xenops lands first (expected non-textual overlap only).","timestamp":1786725866494812001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Patchset 2 pushed on change 1781 (commit 013da02b9c).\n\nCI FAILURE CAUSE (PS1 Verified -1): the cli-reference drift gate — docs/cli-reference.md is DERIVED from the CLI help text, and the new --include-archived usage lines made it stale. Fixed by regenerating with python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py (12 lines).\n\nADVISORY FOLDS (all 4 LLM-Review findings addressed in the same patchset):\n1. (correctness) --include-archived now threads through the repair path too: _repair_run gains include_archived (all 4 _ticket_dirs sites inside it), _run_live_repair and _repair_cli pass it through — 'fsck --repair --include-archived' now repairs what it reports. New test seeds a real SNAPSHOT_INCONSISTENT fault (re-materialized folded source) in a legacy-archived ticket: default dry-run plans nothing, flagged dry-run plans the retire.\n2. (regression) Store-wide metrics stay store-wide: _check_json_validity (per-env authorship tally) and _check_create_events (signed/unsigned presence totals) always walk ALL dirs; include_archived scopes only which findings are REPORTED. Cheap by design: archived tickets are terminally folded, so their walk is snapshot + a few events. New test proves both tallies identical with and without the flag.\n3. (error-handling) _terminal_fold captures the failed compact_cli's stdout+stderr and appends it to the CommandError message.\n4. (tests) New recovery-contract test: forced fold rc=1 → CommandError propagates carrying the fold's output detail, and NO ARCHIVED event or .archived marker is written.\n\nAlso updated the two _ticket_dirs monkeypatch lambdas (repair-pause ownership tests) for the new keyword.\n\nEVIDENCE: test_scan_scoping.py now 13/13 green; +5 targeted mutants on the fold code all KILLED (repair threading dropped, tally walks narrowed x2, error detail dropped, reported-guard inverted) — cumulative 14/14; make lint clean (ratchet new=0 increased=0), make typecheck clean (539 files), adjacent suites 326 passed. Awaiting re-vote on PS2.","timestamp":1786727263502166001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"[operator-attested] Landed via Gerrit change 1781 (3 patchsets), MERGED as 39de64871cccb77606941e2c106a7e60e1c91a0e. Votes: LLM-Review +1 (PASS, 4 advisory findings — ALL folded in PS2: repair-path include_archived threading, store-wide authorship tallies preserved, terminal-fold error detail, recovery-contract test) AND Verified +1 (CI green after regenerating stale docs/cli-reference.md, the PS1 CI failure cause). SUBMITTABLE confirmed pre-submit; status MERGED proves both votes. Implementation: operation-linked terminal fold in leaf.py archive (via compact_cli threshold=0/horizon=0, no compact_txn diff); shared _ticket_dirs(include_archived=False) iterator in fsck_repair.py (marker fast-path + _is_net_archived confirmation); fsck/compact-all default active-only with --include-archived; docs + help updated. Evidence: RED-first 7/10 failed on unmodified code -> 13/13 green; mutation 14/14 killed; make lint + make typecheck clean; 326 adjacent tests pass.","timestamp":1786729385137324001}],"created_at":1786677407480467001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6b092d05-123c-488b-a9c2-7645be28c913","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"226f-6ffe-e9a5-4b61"},{"link_uuid":"10ee24e3-6caa-4367-9da3-54d9eb5dcc72","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9025-fc69-6fea-4e1c"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nStore-wide maintenance walks visit every ticket directory on every run: the fsck scan loops (`_ticket_dirs` iterations in src/rebar/_commands/fsck_scan.py) and the compact-all sweep (src/rebar/_commands/compact.py, whose per-ticket selection is `_scan_snapshot_state`'s own `os.scandir(tracker)` walk invoked by `compact_all_cli`) are O(all tickets ever created). As the store grows, archived tickets — cold, excluded from default `list` — dominate that walk and make routine health checks and sweeps slower for no operational value. `ticket list` already has the pattern to copy: default excludes archived (marker fast-path at reducer/_api.py with compiled-state confirmation) with an explicit `--include-archived` override.\n\n## Approach\nTwo coupled changes, ordered so the default flip is safe:\n1. **Operation-linked terminal fold.** Today `leaf.archive` (src/rebar/_commands/leaf.py) writes only the ARCHIVED event + `.archived` marker — it does NOT fold, so an archived ticket can carry unfolded tail events and the only thing that folds them is a later compact-all walk reaching it. Before scoping that walk to active tickets, make the fold part of the archive operation itself: `rebar archive` performs the ticket's final fold inline right before writing the ARCHIVED event, reusing the existing single-ticket fold path compact_txn already exposes BUT as a TERMINAL fold that bypasses the incremental gates: it passes threshold=0 (fold even a small ticket) and a fold horizon of now (fold the within-horizon tail too), so a just-archived hot ticket — all of whose events are younger than the normal compaction horizon — still gets a complete SNAPSHOT covering every event. If the shared path cannot express that (horizon/threshold baked in), add an explicit terminal/force parameter to it rather than a parallel fold implementation; a ticket with nothing unfolded is a no-op (no empty SNAPSHOT write). This is operation-linked, so it is portable across environments with diverse or NO CI provider — no scheduled sweep is load-bearing. Any later `--include-archived` sweep becomes redundant belt-and-suspenders for tickets archived by pre-change builds, not the sole fold path.\n2. **Active-only default scoping.** Introduce one shared helper (in the module fsck_scan already imports `_ticket_dirs` from) that yields ACTIVE ticket dirs by default — skipping dirs whose net archival state is archived, using the `.archived` marker as the fast-path and the existing `_is_net_archived`-style event-name confirmation, the exact semantics `list` uses — with an `include_archived` flag to yield everything. Switch the fsck scan loops to it, and in compact.py replace `_scan_snapshot_state`'s `os.scandir(tracker)` walk with the shared iterator (matching its existing return contract so `_foldable_event_count` consumers are unchanged), with `compact_all_cli` threading `--include-archived` through to it. Add `--include-archived` to `rebar fsck` and `rebar compact-all` (flag parsing + JSON passthrough; the usage lines live in src/rebar/_cli/help/fsck.txt and compact-all.txt, not in fsck.py). Default = active-only for both: with change 1 in place, an archived ticket really IS folded on its way out, and any deep audit reaches it with the flag.\nBack-out path: the default flip is a one-line revert per command (restore the full walk); change 1 is independently safe to keep since folding at archive time is strictly more converged than folding later.\nPositive rationale: this reuses the archive marker + net-archival semantics that default `list` has proven, rather than inventing a second notion of active.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_commands/leaf.py — archive performs the ticket's terminal fold inline before the ARCHIVED event.\n- src/rebar/_commands/fsck_scan.py — scan loops take the shared active-only iterator; `include_archived` threading.\n- src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py — CLI flag + JSON passthrough.\n- src/rebar/_cli/help/fsck.txt and src/rebar/_cli/help/compact-all.txt — the usage/help text for both commands lives in these files (fsck.py has no usage string); add `--include-archived` there.\n- src/rebar/_commands/compact.py — `_scan_snapshot_state` replaces its `os.scandir` walk with the shared iterator; `compact_all_cli` threads `--include-archived` through; default active-only.\n- tests/unit/test_scan_scoping.py (new) — visited-set coverage both ways + archive-fold sequence test.\n- docs/user-guide.md — document the default, the override, and the archive-time fold.\n\n## Testing\n- Happy path: fixture store with N archived (marker + ARCHIVED event) and M active tickets; default `rebar fsck` and `rebar compact-all --dry-run` visit exactly the M active dirs (assert on the visited set / reported counts); with `--include-archived` they visit N+M.\n- Archive-fold sequence: archive a ticket that has unfolded events, then run DEFAULT `rebar compact-all`; assert the archived ticket's SNAPSHOT covers those events (nothing stranded) even though the default sweep never visited it — the fold happened at archive time.\n- Edge: a ticket dir with a stale marker but NO net-archived state (reverted archive) is still visited by default (the confirmation step, not the marker alone, decides); an archived ticket with a corrupt event file IS reported when `--include-archived` is passed (deep audit still works); a ticket archived by a PRE-change build (unfolded, no inline fold) is folded by a `compact-all --include-archived` run (the belt-and-suspenders path works).\n- Empty store: both commands succeed with zero visits.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `rebar archive` folds the ticket inline (SNAPSHOT covers all its events) before writing ARCHIVED; a just-archived ticket followed by default `compact-all` carries no unfolded events; checked by the sequence test.\n- [x] Default `rebar fsck` and `rebar compact-all` visit only non-archived tickets, and `--include-archived` restores the full walk (including folding legacy archived-but-unfolded tickets); checked by the visited-set and legacy-fold tests.\n- [x] A reverted-archive ticket (stale marker) is never skipped by default; checked by the edge test.\n- [x] Usage lines and docs/user-guide.md name the new flag on both commands and the archive-time fold; checked by --help output in the test and the doc diff.\n- [x] `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1) before close. [operator-attested]","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/leaf.py","reason":"operation-linked terminal fold before ARCHIVED"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck_repair.py","reason":"shared _ticket_dirs iterator + repair-path include_archived threading"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck_scan.py","reason":"scan loops use shared active-only iterator; authorship tallies stay store-wide"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py","reason":"--include-archived flag parsing + JSON passthrough"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact.py","reason":"_scan_snapshot_state via shared iterator; compact-all --include-archived"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/fsck.txt","reason":"usage line for --include-archived"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/compact-all.txt","reason":"usage line for --include-archived"},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"regenerated for new flags"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"documents active-only defaults + archive-time fold"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_scan_scoping.py","reason":"new: scoping, terminal fold, edge cases"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_repair_pause_ownership_heldout.py","reason":"adjusted for repair-path signature change"},{"path":"tests/scripts/graph/test_repair_pause_ownership.py","reason":"adjusted for repair-path signature change"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","fb8a-7363-e406-4e36"],["relates_to","226f-6ffe-e9a5-4b61"],["relates_to","9025-fc69-6fea-4e1c"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"fb8a-7363-e406-4e36","parent_status_uuid":"de19a436-389b-4ca6-bc3c-6612a0503fac","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"bb80-80d0-5f6b-4d45","ticket_type":"story","title":"Active-only scan scoping: fsck and compact-all default to non-archived tickets with --include-archived override","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["254aaf57-5524-4489-a116-2ffa1c22c783","2efc9c2e-2729-4cfa-bf22